# Narrows the Docker build context. None of these enter the image anyway — the
# Dockerfile copies at file/subdirectory level — so the only gain here is build
# time and the amount of data sent to the daemon. `node_modules` matters most:
# the host tree is full of pnpm symlinks whose targets do not exist in the image.
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
.git
.github
*.md
.DS_Store
*.log
*.kubeconfig
kube-configs
